// Template for the app's secrets. This file IS committed; the real one is not.
//
// Setup:
//   1. cp Secrets.example.xcconfig Secrets.xcconfig
//   2. Fill in the two keys below.
//
// Secrets.xcconfig is listed in .gitignore, so your keys stay on your machine.
// Both values are surfaced to the app through Info.plist keys of the same name
// and read at runtime.
//
// Careful: in an xcconfig file "//" starts a comment ANYWHERE on the line,
// including inside a value. A key containing "//" would be silently truncated.
// Neither provider's keys contain it, so this is only a warning — but do not
// add a trailing comment after a key.

// Live speech-to-text, streamed over a WebSocket while you talk.
// Create at https://console.deepgram.com  (API Keys → Create a New API Key)
// Read by DeepgramCredentials.apiKey. WITHOUT THIS, VOICE CAPTURE CANNOT WORK
// on a device: there is no on-device fallback, so the Transcribing screen will
// open and tell the user no key is configured.
DEEPGRAM_API_KEY =

// The rewrite/triage model that turns a raw transcript into a titled capture.
// Create at https://console.groq.com  (API Keys → Create API Key)
// Read by GroqClient.configured. Optional — without it the app still works, it
// just falls back to the local TriageEngine heuristics instead of calling the
// model.
GROQ_API_KEY =
